# The copy the cipher trigger makes is cast during the trigger's resolution (CR 702.99a, 707.12), so the rules on casting apply to
# it. If you can't cast it, you don't (the ruling: it ceases to exist at once, with no later chance). Trait Doctoring is
# encoded on Llanowar Elves. On turn 5 the Elves connect with no Archon of Emeria out, and the copy is offered and cast (the
# positive control). Bot2's Archon of Emeria ("each player can't cast more than one spell each turn") comes down on
# turn 6; on turn 7 Bot1 casts a second Llanowar Elves before combat and then connects with the first. The trigger resolves
# and offers nothing (`! Bot1.Accept`), and the card is still encoded and still exiled (CR 702.99c).

